%SIXMD 1
# @?MAKE - UPDATE TARGETS FROM A MAKEFILE

## DESCRIPTION

MAKE IS THE SMALL NATIVE DAIMOS BUILD DRIVER.  ITS FILE SYNTAX FOLLOWS THE
TRADITIONAL BSD MAKE MODEL WHERE THAT MODEL FITS THE DAIMOS S6REC TEXT AND
RUN/EXEC PROCESS ABI.

USAGE IS 'MAKE [-BKNQS] [-C DIR] [-F FILE] [NAME=VALUE ...] [TARGET ...]'.

RULES HAVE THE FORM:

    TARGET: PREREQUISITE ...
    > COMMAND

S6REC HAS NO TAB CHARACTER, SO '>' IS THE NATIVE RECIPE MARKER.  THIS IS THE
ONE INTENTIONAL SOURCE-SYNTAX DIFFERENCE FROM TRADITIONAL MAKEFILES.

MAKE RECURSIVELY UPDATES PREREQUISITES AND COMPARES THE REAL VFS MTIME36
VALUES.  A MISSING TARGET, A NEWER PREREQUISITE, A PHONY TARGET, OR AN INVALID
NONZERO MTIME CAUSES THE TARGET TO BE REBUILT.  A ZERO-MTIME PREREQUISITE IS
AN UNDATED IMAGE/FILESYSTEM INPUT: IT FORCES A MISSING OR UNDATED TARGET TO BE
BUILT, BUT IS TREATED AS OLDER THAN AN EXISTING TARGET WITH A VALID MTIME.
THIS LETS READ-ONLY SOURCE TREES SHIPPED ON D6FS/TSFS PARTICIPATE IN NORMAL
INCREMENTAL BUILDS.  '-B' REMAINS AVAILABLE WHEN SUCH INPUTS MUST BE FORCED.

RECIPES ARE EXPANDED BY MAKE AND EXECUTED BY '/SYSTEM/EXEC/DSH -C', SO DSH
QUOTING, REDIRECTION, PIPELINES, AND COMMAND SEARCH APPLY TO RECIPE COMMANDS.

WHEN A TARGET NEEDS REBUILDING, MAKE PRINTS 'MAKE: BUILD TARGET' BEFORE
RUNNING ITS RECIPES. EACH RECIPE IS THEN ECHOED UNLESS SILENCED BY '-S' OR
THE LEADING SILENT-RECIPE MARKER. THIS MAKES LONG COMPILER, ASSEMBLER, AND
LINKER STEPS VISIBLE ON A SLOW CONSOLE. '-Q' NEVER PRINTS PROGRESS.

FOR LONG ASSEMBLER/LINKER COMMANDS, PREFIX THE RECIPE WITH '!'. MAKE THEN
EXECUTES THE EXPLICIT ABSOLUTE EXECUTABLE PATH USING RUN V2 WITH SEPARATE
SPACE-DELIMITED ARGUMENTS. THIS DIRECT FORM DOES NOT SUPPORT QUOTING OR
SHELL OPERATORS. THE OVERALL RECIPE LIMIT IS 256 CHARACTERS; RUN V2 LIMITS
EACH ARGUMENT TO 102 CHARACTERS AND THE ARGUMENT COUNT TO 16.

## VARIABLES

THE FOLLOWING ASSIGNMENTS ARE SUPPORTED:

    NAME = VALUE
    NAME := VALUE
    NAME ?= VALUE
    NAME += VALUE

VARIABLE REFERENCES USE '$(NAME)'.  COMMAND-LINE 'NAME=VALUE' ASSIGNMENTS
OVERRIDE MAKEFILE ASSIGNMENTS.  THE STARTUP
ENVIRONMENT IS AVAILABLE AS MAKE VARIABLES.

RECIPES ALSO SUPPORT THE TRADITIONAL AUTOMATIC VARIABLES:

- '$@@' - CURRENT TARGET.
- '$<' - FIRST PREREQUISITE.
- '$?' - PREREQUISITES THAT CAUSED THE TARGET TO BE CONSIDERED OUT OF DATE.
- '$*' - STEM USED BY A SUFFIX TRANSFORMATION RULE.

'$$' EXPANDS TO ONE DOLLAR SIGN.

## RULES

EXPLICIT RULES, MULTIPLE TARGETS, '.PHONY', '.SUFFIXES', AND CLASSIC BSD
SUFFIX TRANSFORMATION RULES SUCH AS '.C.O:' ARE SUPPORTED.  SINGLE-SUFFIX
RULES SUCH AS '.S:' BUILD AN EXTENSIONLESS TARGET FROM 'TARGET.S'.  SUFFIX
RULES ARE USED WHEN THE CORRESPONDING SOURCE FILE EXISTS OR HAS AN EXPLICIT
RULE.

GNU '%' PATTERN RULES, GNU FUNCTIONS, BMAKE VARIABLE MODIFIERS, CONDITIONAL
DIRECTIVES, DOUBLE-COLON RULES, AND DYNAMIC INCLUDE PROCESSING ARE NOT PART OF
THE NATIVE SUBSET.

RECIPE LINES MAY BEGIN WITH '@@' TO SUPPRESS COMMAND ECHO OR '-' TO IGNORE A
NONZERO RECIPE STATUS.

## @?OPTIONS

### @?-F FILE
READ FILE INSTEAD OF 'MAKEFILE'.

### @?-C DIR
CHANGE TO DIR BEFORE READING THE MAKEFILE.

### @?-B
ALWAYS CONSIDER RULE TARGETS OUT OF DATE.

### @?-K
CONTINUE INDEPENDENT WORK AFTER AN ERROR WHEN POSSIBLE.

### @?-N
PRINT RECIPES WITHOUT EXECUTING THEM.

### @?-Q
QUERY WHETHER TARGETS REQUIRE UPDATING WITHOUT RUNNING RECIPES OR PRINTING
THEM. EXIT STATUS 0 MEANS UP TO DATE; 1 MEANS AN UPDATE IS REQUIRED.

### @?-S
DO NOT ECHO RECIPES BEFORE EXECUTION.

## LIMITS

THE RESIDENT IMPLEMENTATION IS BOUNDED: 256 RULES, 768 STORED
PREREQUISITES, 384 STORED RECIPE RECORDS, 64 VARIABLES, 16 REQUESTED TARGETS,
AND A 24576-CHARACTER STRING ARENA. THE SOURCE LINE LIMIT IS 256 CHARACTERS.
THE DIRECT RUN V2 RECIPE FORM ACCEPTS UP TO 16 ARGUMENTS OF AT MOST 102
CHARACTERS EACH. THE SHELL FORM REMAINS SUBJECT TO THE 102-CHARACTER
DSH -C COMMAND ARGUMENT LIMIT. EXCEEDING A LIMIT IS AN ERROR; MAKE DOES NOT
GROW AN UNBOUNDED HEAP GRAPH.

THE NATIVE SINGLE-MAKEFILE KCC BUILD EXERCISES THE LARGER FIXED LIMITS;
OTHER TARGETS REMAIN INDEPENDENT OF THIS BUILD-SPECIFIC CAPACITY.

## @?FILES

### @?MAKEFILE
DEFAULT INPUT FILE.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - REQUESTED TARGETS ARE UP TO DATE OR WERE UPDATED
### @?1 - DEPENDENCY, FILE, OR RECIPE FAILURE
### @?2 - INVALID OPTION, ARGUMENT, OR BOUNDED-PARSER INPUT

## @?SEE ALSO

### @?DSH
### @?STAT
### @?TOUCH
